Sprint-2 M2 ("free wins") was functionally complete but never formally
closed against the 00-shared-contract.md exit gate. This closes it without
touching optimiser behaviour or the committed score (157.0885749337038018263178,
verified unchanged before and after).

- tests/regression/test_monotonicity.py (H2.5, new, test-driven): derives
  s_n = sqrt(term_n * n) from the committed artifacts/best_scores.json and
  asserts s_n <= s_{n+1} across all 200 configs, within a documented
  tolerance. Written test-first: run against a deliberately corrupted
  fixture first (verbatim red captured in LAB_NOTEBOOK.md), then against
  the real, unmodified file (green). A second test pins the tolerance
  below CLEARANCE_EPS so it can't be loosened to mask a real regression.

- Mutation spot-check (H2.6, §2.5): flipped the comparison operator in the
  new test, re-ran against the same corrupted fixture, confirmed the suite
  still failed (for a different, documented reason). Reverted.

- H2.4 (insertion zero-growth count) measured for the first time: 9 of 199
  configs (n = 10, 13, 21, 22, 25, 26, 36, 37, 38) admit a zero-growth
  insertion. Refutes the predicted >=15 without falsifying (floor was 5).
  Also surfaces that solve_portfolio never calls grow_layout or
  ratchet_layouts in production — recorded in DECISIONS.md as an explicit
  input for M3, not assumed away.

- LAB_NOTEBOOK.md: single merged M2.0 entry replaced with one entry per
  H2.1-H2.6 using the sec 2.3 template.

- DECISIONS.md: addendum recording the insertion/ratchet wiring gap and the
  tolerance-as-decision rationale.

Full Gate re-run clean: ruff format/check, mypy, lint-imports, pytest
(57 passed). reference/ untouched. artifacts/best_scores.json byte-identical.
